{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "35733888",
      "title": "Working with Index Routes",
      "sourceHash": "7432b1da54d0e1d500e74cc26309a3c9424876fcd548a19bd82cffbf35e98367",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.07,
          "end": 3.99,
          "en": "Now, related to what you learned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.99,
          "end": 6.42,
          "en": "about relative and absolute paths,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.42,
          "end": 8.07,
          "en": "at least kind of related,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.07,
          "end": 9.87,
          "en": "there's one special property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 9.87,
          "end": 11.85,
          "en": "you can add to your route definitions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 11.85,
          "end": 14.49,
          "en": "to some route definitions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 14.49,
          "end": 17.28,
          "en": "And that is a special property that would, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 17.28,
          "end": 19.47,
          "en": "apply to the homepage here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 19.47,
          "end": 22.983,
          "en": "What's special about this homepage route definition?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 24.12,
          "end": 26.67,
          "en": "Well, in the end, it doesn't have a path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 26.67,
          "end": 30.24,
          "en": "Instead, the homepage should be loaded for the same path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 30.24,
          "end": 33.15,
          "en": "as we have it here on the parent route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 33.15,
          "end": 35.04,
          "en": "We have two different routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 35.04,
          "end": 37.833,
          "en": "because we want to have that wrapping layout, though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 38.79,
          "end": 40.62,
          "en": "But it is quite common that you might have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 40.62,
          "end": 45.15,
          "en": "such a wrapping layout route, as we have it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 45.15,
          "end": 47.07,
          "en": "And then you have one child route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 47.07,
          "end": 49.57,
          "en": "that should be loaded for the parent's route path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 50.58,
          "end": 54.48,
          "en": "Now, you could solve it like this by adding no path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 54.48,
          "end": 58.17,
          "en": "But alternatively, you can add the special index property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 58.17,
          "end": 59.463,
          "en": "and set this to true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 60.3,
          "end": 63.66,
          "en": "This turns this route into a so-called index route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 63.66,
          "end": 65.82,
          "en": "which simply means it's the default route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 65.82,
          "end": 68.82,
          "en": "that should be displayed if the parent route's path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 68.82,
          "end": 70.053,
          "en": "is currently active.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 70.92,
          "end": 75.87,
          "en": "So it will not be loaded for products or products/productId.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 75.87,
          "end": 78.75,
          "en": "But if we're on just /nothing in this case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 78.75,
          "end": 82.11,
          "en": "this index route will be activated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 82.11,
          "end": 82.95,
          "en": "And if we save that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 82.95,
          "end": 85.53,
          "en": "we therefore get the same behavior as before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 85.53,
          "end": 87.75,
          "en": "The application works as before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 87.75,
          "end": 90.12,
          "en": "but this is now a different way of solving this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 90.12,
          "end": 94.53,
          "en": "And you should be aware of this feature called index routes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 94.53,
          "end": 96.84,
          "en": "which allows you to define the default route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 96.84,
          "end": 100.233,
          "en": "that should be loaded if the parent routes path is active.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 101.88,
          "end": 104.31,
          "en": "Of course, you don't have to have index routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 104.31,
          "end": 106.95,
          "en": "It depends on your use case and application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 106.95,
          "end": 109.47,
          "en": "but often you want such default routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 109.47,
          "end": 112.2,
          "en": "And that is how you could solve it alternatively",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 112.2,
          "end": 113.973,
          "en": "to adding this empty path here.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}